***************************
* SET UP THE INITIAL DATA *
***************************

NAME          LRW1A

*   Problem :
*   --------

*   Fit a data set using regularized logistic regresion

*   The problem is to minimize the cross-entropy function for the
*   class label y which may be l or u (>l) is

*    C(w) =  - 1/|samples| sum_i (samples) 
*                [(y_i - l)/(u - l) log p(w,x_i) +
*                 (u - y_i)/(u - l) log(1 - p(w,x_i))],

*   where p(x,w) = 1/(1 + exp(-l(x,w))) 
*   [  => 1 - p(x,w) = exp(-l(x,w) / (1 + exp(-l(x,w)))  ]
*   and l(x,w) = sum_j (features) w_j x_j,

*   with an added regularization 

*    sigma sum_j (features) x_j^2 / ( 1 + x_j^2 ) 

*   Source: the w1a dataset from the LIBSVM collection

*    https://www.csie.ntu.edu.tw/~cjlin/libsvmtools/datasets/

*   See
*   Chih-Chung Chang and Chih-Jen Lin, 
*   LIBSVM : a library for support vector machines. 
*   ACM Trans. Intelligent Systems & Technology, 2:27:1--27:27, 2011.

*   SIF input: Nick Gould, Jan 2023

*   classification OUR2-AN-300-0

*   Number of features (explanatory variables)

 IE N                   300

*   Number of samples (categorical variables)

 IE M                   2477

*   categories

 RE LOWER               -1.0
 RE UPPER               1.0

*   regularization weight

 RE SIGMA               0.01

*   other parameter definitions

 IE 1                   1
 RE ONE                 1.0
 RI RM        M
 R- RANGE     UPPER                    LOWER
 R* SCALE     RM                       RANGE

*  categorical variables

